.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt KERNEL-PATCHES 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kernel-patches
.Nd FreeBSD kernel patches for GPU drivers on arm64 and on Ampere Altra
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm sh
.Pa kernel-patches/apply.sh
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl R
.Ar srcdir
.Op Ar patch ...
.Nm sh
.Pa kernel-patches/apply.sh
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Pa kernel-patches
directory of nvidia-gb10-freebsd holds four patches to the
.Fx
kernel source, applied with
.Xr patch 1
in the order of the
.Pa series
file:
.Bl -tag -width "0004"
.It Pa 0001-linuxkpi-arm64-write-combining.diff
On arm64, LinuxKPI maps
.Fn ioremap_wc ,
.Fn pgprot_writecombine
and
.Vt io_mapping
as Normal non-cacheable instead of the cacheable write-through
.Dv VM_MEMATTR_WRITE_COMBINING ,
and makes
.Fn memcpy_toio ,
.Fn memcpy_fromio
and
.Fn memset_io
use only naturally aligned accesses.
Needed on every arm64 machine with a drm-kmod driver.
It changes headers only: the GPU modules must be rebuilt against the
patched tree.
.It Pa 0002-linuxkpi-altra-erratum-82288.diff
LinuxKPI maps write-combining and uncached PCIe memory as Device-nGnRE on
an Ampere Altra (erratum 82288).
.It Pa 0003-arm64-kernel-alignment-fixup.diff
Emulates kernel-mode alignment faults of general-purpose loads and stores
and
.Li DC ZVA
on Device memory instead of panicking with
.Dq Misaligned access from kernel space! .
On by default only on an Ampere Altra.
It handles kernel-mode faults only: a program that makes an unaligned
access or a
.Li DC ZVA
on a Device mapping gets
.Dv SIGBUS
.Pq Dv BUS_ADRALN .
.It Pa 0004-pci-host-generic-altra-ecam.diff
.Xr pci 4
configuration reads on Ampere Altra host bridges are made as aligned 32-bit
reads.
Adds the test
.Pa tests/sys/pci/pci_host_generic_quirks_test .
.El
.Pp
An Ampere Altra is recognized by its ACPI MCFG table: OEM ID
.Dq Ampere
and an OEM table ID starting with
.Dq Altra
for 0002 and 0003; OEM table ID
.Dq Altra
with OEM revision 1 for 0004.
On other machines 0002, 0003 and 0004 do nothing.
.Pp
.Nm apply.sh
dry-runs every selected patch against
.Ar srcdir
first and stops, changing nothing, if any patch would be rejected, would
only apply with fuzz, or would create a file that is already there with
other contents.
A patch that is already applied is skipped.
It writes only the files the patches name, inside
.Ar srcdir ,
and no backup or reject files.
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-R"
.It Fl n
Dry run only.
.It Fl R
Take the patches out again, last one first.
.It Fl h
Print the usage.
.El
.Pp
With
.Ar patch
arguments, only those patches of the series are used, still in series
order.
.Sh LOADER TUNABLES
These are also read-write
.Xr sysctl 8
variables.
.Bl -tag -width "compat.linuxkpi.altra_82288"
.It Va compat.linuxkpi.altra_82288
From 0002.
.Li -1
(default) automatic: mode
.Li 1
on an Altra;
.Li 0
off;
.Li 1
kernel mappings use Device-nGnRE;
.Li 2
kernel and user
.Pq Xr mmap 2
mappings use Device-nGnRE.
Mode
.Li 2
is for testing only: a program that makes an unaligned access or a large
memset into GPU memory it mapped can get
.Dv SIGBUS ,
and a
.Xr read 2
or
.Xr write 2
from such a buffer at an unaligned address can fail with
.Dv EFAULT .
Whether the machine is an Altra is decided once, when LinuxKPI
initialises; on other machines the setting is ignored and no mapping is
changed.
The variable exists from boot when LinuxKPI is built into the kernel (arm64 GENERIC), otherwise once
.Pa linuxkpi.ko
is loaded.
.It Va machdep.kern_align_fixup
From 0003.
.Li -1
(default) automatic: on when the ACPI MCFG names an Altra, off elsewhere;
.Li 0
off;
.Li 1
on.
The ACPI MCFG is read once at boot, before any driver attaches.
Writing
.Li -1
at run time goes back to the automatic choice.
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
These are read-only.
.Bl -tag -width "compat.linuxkpi.altra_82288_active"
.It Va compat.linuxkpi.altra_82288_active
From 0002.
The mode in effect:
.Li 0
(off, or not an Altra),
.Li 1
or
.Li 2 .
.It Va machdep.kern_align_fixup_active
From 0003.
.Li 1
when the fixup is in effect,
.Li 0
when it is not.
.It Va machdep.kern_align_fixups
From 0003.
The number of kernel accesses emulated since boot.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "kernel-patches/README.md" -compact
.It Pa kernel-patches/series
the patch order and the
.Fx
commits each patch was checked against
.It Pa kernel-patches/README.md
the step-by-step guide: matching source, apply, build, install as
.Pa /boot/kernel.patched ,
a
.Xr nextboot 8
test, making it the default, going back, updates
.It Pa /boot/kernel.patched
where the README installs the patched kernel
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm apply.sh
exits 0 when every patch was applied, reverted or skipped, or the dry run
passed; 1 when a patch does not apply or
.Ar srcdir
is not a
.Fx
source tree; 2 on a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check, apply and build:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sh kernel-patches/apply.sh -n ~/src/freebsd
sh kernel-patches/apply.sh ~/src/freebsd
cd ~/src/freebsd
env PATH=/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin MAKEOBJDIRPREFIX=~/obj \e
    make -j"$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu)" buildkernel KERNCONF=GENERIC
.Ed
.Pp
Check the result after booting the patched kernel on an Altra:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysctl machdep.kern_align_fixup_active machdep.kern_align_fixups
dmesg | grep -e 'alignment-fault fixup' -e '32-bit config space'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patch 1 ,
.Xr pci 4 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr build 7 ,
.Xr acpidump 8 ,
.Xr freebsd-update 8 ,
.Xr nextboot 8
.Sh CAVEATS
The patched kernel matches one
.Fx
version.
After every update of the base system rebuild it from the matching source,
or boot the stock kernel; see the README.
.Pp
The patches are not part of
.Fx .
.Sh BUGS
Report problems at
.Lk https://github.com/cloudbsdorg/nvidia-gb10-freebsd/issues
